Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Bosonic Algebra, Stabilizers, and Interferometers: Keynote Examples\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->171623919,ExpressionUUID->"6d4b35a1-5eba-e261-3545-ed30b96cf6d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Bosonic algebra.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Wolfram QuantumFramework now computes exactly in the Weyl algebra of light \
and oscillators: it disentangles squeezers, beam splitters and even cubic \
exponentials into normal-ordered closed forms, identities that physicists \
otherwise derive by hand from commutators, valid at every photon number and \
never truncated to a finite matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1606804240,ExpressionUUID->"35b09861-2830-44c3-2166-ea2cc5ad00e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Stabilizer formalism.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Wolfram QuantumFramework runs Clifford circuits on the stabilizer tableau, \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aa34e1c-8bd0-3ee0-6217-faf3bf036b71"],
 " Pauli generators instead of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "463c6386-2b69-8d0c-1a8e-0db8954265a0"],
 " amplitudes, so a thousand-qubit state takes milliseconds and its \
entanglement comes out as an exact integer from linear algebra over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\|01d53d", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08d0737f-2a48-82f5-66f1-f72f788347ab"],
 ". When a non-Clifford T gate arrives, the same object switches to an exact \
superposition of stabilizer states instead of failing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1787170966,ExpressionUUID->"0ebe674e-8808-3928-54ad-5d276f25552b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["QuantumInterferometer.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " In Wolfram QuantumFramework a beam splitter is an SU(2) rotation of the \
photon modes, so its photon-counting amplitudes are Wigner D-functions \
returned symbolically with the photon numbers themselves left as variables. \
One exact formula covers Hong-Ou-Mandel interference for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6bb0ff29-7a4c-f121-6abc-747823fdc722"],
 ", where other photonics software computes one photon count at a time, \
numerically."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1617143183,ExpressionUUID->"57ac0905-17cb-d594-7b26-21f4df370fa9"],

Cell["Install the QuantumFramework:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002645293902192*^9, 4.002645299974999*^9}},
 CellID->1175228907,ExpressionUUID->"5cbaa588-6144-da35-66b9-e0fd0c5c367c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"PacletInstall", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<https://www.wolfr.am/DevWQCF\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ForceVersionInstall", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"",
   "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->1304387619,ExpressionUUID->"042d8526-542b-2564-4f69-b4838dee78e9"],

